{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/443195-saibot-s-new-devotion-thread","id":443195,"title":"Saibot's New Devotion Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T16:03:07-07:00","id":443195,"title":"Saibot's New Devotion Thread","content":"Hello there!<br /> <br /> We have created some custom Devotions for our current Chronicle and so I thought it might be nice to share them here. Many of these are inspired by 1e Devotions or similar sources. This will be noted. It is quite possible I will create more in the future, in which case I will also post them here. As always, ideas and criticism welcome. I also encourage you to post ideas for other Devotions which I might turn into proper stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Aura of Hesitation</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Majesty 2 <b>or</b> Nightmare 2<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Majesty and Nightmare are fearsome powers, affecting a target\u2019s perception and emotions. With this Devotion a vampire can amplify her supernatural auras of adoration or dread to make foes doubt themselves and cause them to hesitate for a few critical moments. They fear or adore the vampire too much for rash action. This hesitation is often enough to destroy or subjugate attackers before they become a true threat. Kindred can develop this Devotion with the requisite level of either Majesty or Nightmare. Its effects are the same, but the vampire must buy it related to one Discipline. This Devotion enhances the effect of Awe or Dread Presence when activated. Anyone hostile to the vampire who is affected by the vampire\u2019s Awe or Dread Presence suffers the vampire\u2019s Majesty or Nightmare as an Initiative penalty. If someone affected by this power somehow becomes unaffected by Awe or Dread Presence (for example by successfully Lashing Out) he also becomes unaffected by this Devotion.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn.<br /> <br /> (NB: This power is inspired by the suggested effect of Majesty in combat <b>from Danse Macabre</b>)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Destructive Might</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Vigor 5, Resilience 3<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Some vampires manage to push their supernatural strength even beyond mastery of Vigor. Their punches and kicks become able to literally tear off limbs and pulverize bones. Such power requires extraordinary toughness as well to avoid breaking even the Kindred\u2019s strange physique. This Devotion can be reflexively activated after activating the Vigor weapon bonus (for a total cost of 2 Vitae). The vampire\u2019s Athletics, Brawl and Weaponry attacks deal Aggravated damage to mortals and Lethal to vampires. Any mundane weapon used with this Devotion immediately breaks after a successful attack.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 4 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> (NB: This power is a port of the Devotion of the same name from <b>Ancient Mysteries</b>)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sea</b><b> of Stone</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Protean 2, Vigor 2<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae or more (see below)<br /> Dice Pool: Strength + Resolve + Protean<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> With this Devotion a vampire can literally force himself through solid substances, entering one side and exiting another, fusing with them for a moment. When used on thin obstacles (doors, windows, etc) he simply has to spend Vitae equal to the obstacle\u2019s Durability (minimum 1) and then travels through it as an Instant Action. For thicker obstacles, he first need to merge with it as per Unmarked Grave (paying the regular cost) and then spend 1 Vitae per turn of travel. He can travel a number of yards equal to his Protean in a single turn. Once he reaches his destination he exits on the other side as if he were exiting his Unmarked Grave. On an Exceptional Success on the activation roll the vampire may travel two turns without Vitae cost. This Devotion can be used to avoid damage caused through destruction of one\u2019s Unmarked Grave by moving your exact position.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Preternatural Instinct</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Animalism 2, Celerity 2<br /> Cost: 2 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> By connecting to her Beast\u2019s primal instincts through Animalism and combining it with the incredible speed of Celerity a vampire can anticipate an attacker\u2019s shots and dodge them as she would a punch or blade. Such a vampire is a hard target even for experienced shooters. Once this Devotion is activated the vampire can apply her Defense against firearms attacks. Multiple attacks against the vampire still reduce her Defense as normal. This Devotion lasts for the entire Scene.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> (NB: This power is inspired by the abilities displayed by werewolves in some of their forms.)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wicked Grasp</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Nightmare 1, Vigor 1<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> With this Devotion a Nosferatu can enhance the power of his Dread Presence. Anyone grabbed by him suffers visions of the Haunt\u2019s arms turning into huge snakes, him being a giant mass of worms, a creature of disgusting malleable clay or something equally horrifying. These hallucinations make it hard for the victim to resist this terrifying struggle. After this Devotion is activated anyone affected by Dread Presence who finds themselves in a grapple with the Nosferatu suffers his Nightmare as a penalty to their contested Strength + Brawl to overpower. If someone affected by this power somehow becomes unaffected by Dread Presence (for example by successfully Lashing Out) she also becomes unaffected by this Devotion. This lasts for the entire Scene.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> (NB: This power is a port of the Devotion of the same name from <b>The Beast That Haunts The Blood</b>)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 03-15-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T21:47:34-07:00","id":452275,"title":"","content":"Preternatural Instincts is already in the core book. Its called Quicken Sight. Its a Celerity+Auspex (Auspex is the Beasts Instincts/senses discipline. Animalism is more akin to dominate, its control).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:09:49-07:00","id":452693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/443195-saibot-s-new-devotion-thread?p=452275#post452275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Preternatural Instincts is already in the core book. Its called Quicken Sight. Its a Celerity+Auspex (Auspex is the Beasts Instincts/senses discipline. Animalism is more akin to dominate, its control).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Quicken Sight is per turn, not per scene and has other benefits.<br /> <br /> As for Animalism, I went with the way it was written in <b>Danse Macabre</b> and <b>Ancient Mysteries</b>, which supports the idea of Animalism also being about instints. Which is also supported in Animalism 4 and 5 in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}